{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_99fb369f209c07d12b7b1ee9e4962c6f4328c5fd2be596fe0055f682510ba296"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: recipe contributions should use the provided template, start from the problem being solved, include a GIF demo, give step-by-step setup instructions, cross-reference related recipes, and be self-contained."}],"claim_ids":["clm_99fb369f209c07d12b7b1ee9e4962c6f4328c5fd2be596fe0055f682510ba296"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","id":"pg_6f7b2e1894685cafb3a3b1dd7fe7fc17","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sudo-tee-opencode-nvim-docs-readme-md-636a26425227-b1dd7fe7fc17.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3a0469724adf5ce2a91cf8903773862e"],"title":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim/docs/README.md @ 636a26425227","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","id":"pg_8dcac85ede9859d18ec33aece2a2ad6b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sudo-tee-opencode-nvim-docs-performance-audit-md-636a26425227-3aece2a2ad6b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_110484caf31e5f1093a89c021f7f3fc4"],"title":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim/docs/performance-audit.md @ 636a26425227","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_09b4d6767cebabeb82e24c87f463cba1493e545dde58a8c22913a5642e0944e6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README cautions that the plugin is in early development, may have bugs and breaking changes, and is not recommended for production use yet."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0b6999515845995de780c194625a6db8ab91f843f97de0b91f941d198394b896"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin requires the Opencode CLI v0.6.3 or newer to be installed and available."},{"claim_ids":["clm_158e498610f93c3c97771a523d44ae78febef2ee186892d371e9bb64011be9ce"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"With ui.persist_state true (default), toggle hides/restores the UI keeping buffers in memory for fast restore; false fully tears down and recreates buffers, and close() always fully closes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3dc2f3604b3ce498691173863074b58ea065bc4d92f8ab88a493b8a3bea0fba0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Permission requests can be answered via a dialog (j/k plus <CR> or number keys), commands like :Opencode permission accept/accept_all/deny, or API functions mapping to once/always/reject responses."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3effa5b394bd24207d07e90b610c7217b5e339ebd163a1216fad1507b3ebcefc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Favorite models, toggled with <C-f> in the model picker, show a star icon, sort to the top, and persist across Neovim sessions; the plugin respects the OpenCode CLI storage format."},{"claim_ids":["clm_401bcd08fe6b427b6b44c8bc8619e9739adeb82b5de8cd12a97e768952ed0b27"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An experimental quick buffer chat feature (<leader>o/) chats using the current buffer context, capturing visual selections or the current line, and the AI's quick edits are applied by the plugin."},{"claim_ids":["clm_43efeec5a5fa4211c5bd210c008c47016dede64629a6ad312a7ca01b0a0d77aa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Opencode issues permission requests for potentially destructive operations (file edits, reverts, shell commands, persistent tool access); requests appear inline and must be answered before the action proceeds."},{"claim_ids":["clm_49ca772a38e6eff8ef8ae591fa0ce3d07c2bbbbc0c1d79b39fe631c0b77879b7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A dedicated chat panel window inside Neovim shows previous messages and responses and uses workspace/editor state as context for iterating on code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_53236c67f284ba1a6764c1985b9b940aaca713a266162841b775a27d8c60e1df"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Recommended lazy.nvim setup lists render-markdown.nvim as a dependency, with optional blink.cmp or nvim-cmp for completion and snacks.nvim, telescope, fzf-lua, or mini.nvim as optional pickers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_731b3fd7396788213ab1336c8e49f67a9e2133d389da17aaac53912c914a6f8f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prompts can be run with options overriding the agent, model, or per-prompt context types (current_file, selection, diagnostics, cursor_data), e.g. agent=plan context.current_file.enabled=false."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8b0c50c736686a6886ae1de5a5cb4907fb7ff23cc047fecab1617b8c06ec74eb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The model picker sorts favorites first (by favoriting order), then recently used models, then others alphabetically; variant selection per model is remembered for future use."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8f8a01e5f8290537cb72641aee6f97caf91a4521a0d43f7c73e98c246df5bab6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The server configuration supports custom/external opencode servers with url, port, timeout, spawn_command, auto_kill, path_map, and Basic-auth username/password with env-var fallbacks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8fe2647361b7676fdf1eab07e073f1c931dc290c5f4773295045f7a0faf0f656"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Editor context is automatically captured for conversations, including current file, visual selection, mentioned files, diagnostics, and cursor position/line content."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9dfbb7ff2f78e3f6ff3295ed494798bf0e0d7727197d55f2a9432624c6574eba"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin bridges Neovim and the opencode AI agent, providing a chat interface that captures editor context such as the current file and selections, with persistent sessions tied to the workspace."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d5621af849e40a0dd4d13787851b4189f0188804f6085142a3652b2004c20a61"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Actions are reachable via default keymaps (e.g. <leader>og toggle), user commands (e.g. :Opencode open input), and Lua API functions such as require('opencode.api').toggle()."}],"claim_ids":["clm_09b4d6767cebabeb82e24c87f463cba1493e545dde58a8c22913a5642e0944e6","clm_0b6999515845995de780c194625a6db8ab91f843f97de0b91f941d198394b896","clm_158e498610f93c3c97771a523d44ae78febef2ee186892d371e9bb64011be9ce","clm_3dc2f3604b3ce498691173863074b58ea065bc4d92f8ab88a493b8a3bea0fba0","clm_3effa5b394bd24207d07e90b610c7217b5e339ebd163a1216fad1507b3ebcefc","clm_401bcd08fe6b427b6b44c8bc8619e9739adeb82b5de8cd12a97e768952ed0b27","clm_43efeec5a5fa4211c5bd210c008c47016dede64629a6ad312a7ca01b0a0d77aa","clm_49ca772a38e6eff8ef8ae591fa0ce3d07c2bbbbc0c1d79b39fe631c0b77879b7","clm_53236c67f284ba1a6764c1985b9b940aaca713a266162841b775a27d8c60e1df","clm_731b3fd7396788213ab1336c8e49f67a9e2133d389da17aaac53912c914a6f8f","clm_8b0c50c736686a6886ae1de5a5cb4907fb7ff23cc047fecab1617b8c06ec74eb","clm_8f8a01e5f8290537cb72641aee6f97caf91a4521a0d43f7c73e98c246df5bab6","clm_8fe2647361b7676fdf1eab07e073f1c931dc290c5f4773295045f7a0faf0f656","clm_9dfbb7ff2f78e3f6ff3295ed494798bf0e0d7727197d55f2a9432624c6574eba","clm_d5621af849e40a0dd4d13787851b4189f0188804f6085142a3652b2004c20a61"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","id":"pg_ee990a78265a521ea79eb6512b18dcbe","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sudo-tee-opencode-nvim-readme-md-636a26425227-b6512b18dcbe.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a2bbf80420c95f7ca096a720cb368939"],"title":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim/REA